# Version control / CI
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Frontend — irrelevant to the Go build, large build context
portals/

# Secrets and key material. Every path here is gitignored, so a CI build from a
# clean checkout never sees it; these rules make a local `docker build` behave
# the same way instead of copying a developer's credentials into the build
# context (and, with cache-to mode=max, into the shared layer cache).
.env
.env.*
idp/
certs/

# Live service configs hold literal credentials (client secrets, SMTP/SMS
# tokens) and are gitignored. Only the committed *.example.json templates are
# baked; deployments supply the real files via ConfigMap or bind mount, which is
# the documented contract for /app/configs.
configs/*.json
!configs/*.example.json

# Runtime data — must never be baked into the image
bucket/

# Dev-only trees and local tooling the build never reads. NOTE: do not add
# external-integration/ here — internal/bootstrap and internal/tasks/plugins
# import it, so it is a build input.
test/
deployments/
docs/
Makefile
compose*.yml
go.work
go.work.sum
coverage.out

# Docs & meta
*.md
LICENSE

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build output
/out/
*.test
